BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fluxus-cpga-prize-frieze-london-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fluxus-CPGA Prize at Frieze London 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fluxus-CPGA Prize at Frieze London\, a collaboration betwee
 n Fluxus Art Projects\, the Comite Professionnel des Galeries d'Art and Fr
 ieze London\, supports talent from the French art scene and promotes its v
 isibility internationally. It also celebrates the relationship between art
 ists and their galleries: the GBP 15\,000 prize is shared between the two.
  WHO APPLIES: galleries of any nationality exhibiting at Frieze London 202
 6\, presenting the work of one French or French-based artist on their stan
 d\; artists cannot apply directly. HOW TO APPLY: via the Google Form linke
 d from the apply page\, with gallery contact information\, the artist's na
 me and number of works presented\, an artist biography (200 words)\, a gal
 lery description (200 words) and 1 to 2 images. Free of charge. Previous l
 aureates include Daiga Grantina (Emalin\, 2025)\, Stephanie Saade (Marfa' 
 Projects\, 2024) and Josefa Ntjam (Nicoletti\, 2023)\; jurors have include
 d Hans Ulrich Obrist\, Zoe Whitley\, Catherine Wood and Valeria Napoleone.
  Deadline 28 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fluxus Art Projects\, with t
 he Comite Professionnel des Galeries d'Art and Frieze London\nLocation: Fr
 ieze London\, Regent's Park\, London\, UK (October 2026). Galleries of any
  nationality can apply\, provided they present the work of a French or Fre
 nch-based artist on their stand.\nAward: GBP 15\,000 prize\, shared betwee
 n the artist and their gallery. Participation is free of charge.\nDuration
 : Awarded during Frieze London in October 2026\n\nMore: https://fluxusartp
 rojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://fluxusartprojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Frieze London\, Regent's Park\, London\, UK (October 2026). Galler
 ies of any nationality can apply\, provided they present the work of a Fre
 nch or French-based artist on their stand.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fluxus-prize-art-basel-paris-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fluxus Prize at Art Basel Paris 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fluxus Prize at Art Basel Paris\, from Fluxus Art Projects\
 , supports talent from the British art scene and promotes its visibility i
 nternationally\, honouring the relationship between artists and their gall
 eries: the EUR 15\,000 prize is shared between the two. This edition is su
 pported by Belinda de Gaudemar and Laurent Issaurat. WHO APPLIES: gallerie
 s of any nationality exhibiting at Art Basel Paris 2026 in the Galleries o
 r Premise sectors\, presenting the work of one British or UK-based artist\
 ; artists cannot apply directly. HOW TO APPLY: by email to visual.arts[at]
 institut-francais.org.uk with gallery contact information\, the artist's n
 ame and number of works presented\, an artist biography (200 words)\, a ga
 llery description (200 words) and 1 to 2 images. Free of charge. Previous 
 laureates include Olu Ogunnaike (Hollybush Gardens\, 2025) and Jesse Darli
 ng (Sultana\, 2024)\; jurors have included Hans Ulrich Obrist\, Caroline B
 ourgeois and Daria de Beauvais. Deadline 29 September 2026.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Fluxus Art Projects\, with Art Basel Paris\nLocation: Art Basel Paris\,
  France (October 2026). Galleries of any nationality can apply\, provided 
 they present the work of one British or UK-based artist in the Galleries o
 r Premise sectors.\nAward: EUR 15\,000 prize\, shared between the artist a
 nd their gallery. Participation is free of charge.\nDuration: Awarded duri
 ng Art Basel Paris in October 2026\n\nMore: https://fluxusartprojects.com/
 apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fluxusartprojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Art Basel Paris\, France (October 2026). Galleries of any national
 ity can apply\, provided they present the work of one British or UK-based 
 artist in the Galleries or Premise sectors.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:script-pipeline-first-look-project-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Script Pipeline: First Look Project 2026 (screenplay and 
 TV pilot contest)
DESCRIPTION:The 15th annual First Look Project from Script Pipeline searche
 s for higher-concept material across six categories: feature screenplays i
 n Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, and Horror and Thriller\, plus hour
  and half-hour original TV pilots. Unlike Script Pipeline's Screenwriting 
 and TV Writing contests\, entries are judged on both writing ability and m
 arket potential\, in addition to originality of concept\; a script that st
 ill needs refining can win if the story could stand out in the current lan
 dscape\, as the aim is a first look at the next buzzworthy specs before th
 ey hit the market. GUIDELINES: screenplays must be feature length\; genres
  without a listed category go to the closest one (Fantasy\, Western or Adv
 enture under Action and Sci-Fi\; Crime and Mystery under Thriller). TV pil
 ots run roughly 30 to 60 pages\, all genres accepted including animation a
 nd genre hybrids. The script must not be under an option or shopping agree
 ment at the time of entry\, and the same script cannot compete in multiple
  categories. CIRCULATION: Script Pipeline's industry relationships (Bellev
 ue Productions\, LBI Entertainment\, Hungry Man\, Alibi Management and oth
 ers) have led to writers signed\, specs sold and films produced. Regular d
 eadline 30 September 2026\; late deadline 15 October\; extended deadline 3
 0 October. Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Script Pip
 eline\nLocation: Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pip
 eline is based in Los Angeles\, US.\nAward: USD 15\,000 in total prizes ac
 ross six winners: USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of four screenplay genr
 e categories (Action and Sci-Fi\, Comedy\, Drama\, Horror and Thriller) an
 d USD 2\,500 to the winner of each of two TV pilot categories (hour and ha
 lf-hour). All winners also receive long-term circulation to Script Pipelin
 e's industry network of producers\, managers\, agents and directors\, 1-on
 -1 development assistance from Script Pipeline execs\, additional script r
 eviews and consideration of other material\, career guidance and mentorshi
 p\, and invitations to private Symposium events. Entry fee: USD 60 at the 
 regular deadline\, rising to USD 65 (late\, 15 October) and USD 70 (extend
 ed\, 30 October).\nDuration: Winners announced 15 December 2026.\n\nMore: 
 https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://scriptpipeline.com/contest/first-look-project?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\; open to writers worldwide. Script Pipeline is 
 based in Los Angeles\, US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:we-are-human-festival-call-for-films-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: We Are Human Festival 2026: Call for Films (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:Call for short films (1-10 minutes) involving human/AI hybrid c
 reation\, from the We Are Human Foundation in Paris. Three cash awards: Gr
 and Prix EUR 5\,000\, Best Screenplay EUR 3\,000\, and an Ethics Award EUR
  2\,000. ELIGIBILITY: international\, applicants 18+\; films must have bee
 n completed after 1 June 2025 and involve human/AI hybrid creation\; a man
 datory Ethics Notebook accompanies each submission. No submission fee. Fes
 tival screening at Forum des images\, Paris\, on 24 November 2026. Apply v
 ia FilmFreeway\; deadline 30 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: We Are Human
  Foundation\nLocation: Paris\, France (Forum des images screening 24 Novem
 ber 2026)\nAward: Grand Prix EUR 5\,000\; Best Screenplay EUR 3\,000\; Eth
 ics Award EUR 2\,000. No submission fee.\nDuration: Annual short-film fest
 ival (screening 24 November 2026)\n\nMore: https://wearehuman.foundation/e
 n/call-for-films/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://wearehuman.foundation/en/call-for-films/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Forum des images screening 24 November 2026)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rtm-pitch-iffr-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: RTM Pitch 2026 (IFFR)
DESCRIPTION:Eighth edition of RTM Pitch\, IFFR's open call for Rotterdam fi
 lm talent. Submit a plan for a film between 5 and 20 minutes long\; a jury
  of film experts and IFFR programmers selects one filmmaker to receive EUR
  25\,000 to realise the film (with coaching and an IFFR 2028 premiere) and
  a runner-up to receive a EUR 5\,000 development budget co-funded by QISSA
 . All filmmakers are welcome\; this edition especially encourages genre fi
 lms (horror\, science fiction\, thriller\, fantasy) that use genre convent
 ions for a distinctive personal vision. Submit a written film plan (story\
 , setting\, team\, budget and financing\, cinematography vision\, with opt
 ional supporting material) or a video pitch of no more than three minutes 
 (Vimeo or YouTube link) via the application form. Deadline: Sunday 30 Augu
 st 2026\, 23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: International Film Festival Rotterd
 am (IFFR)\nLocation: Rotterdam\, Netherlands\nAward: EUR 25\,000 for the w
 inner (EUR 20\,000 from the City of Rotterdam\, EUR 5\,000 from VEVAM Fond
 s) to realise the film\, plus tailored coaching and an IFFR premiere\; a r
 unner-up receives a EUR 5\,000 development budget co-funded by QISSA. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: Short film of 5 to 20 minutes\; winning film pr
 emieres during RTM Day at IFFR 2028\n\nMore: https://iffr.com/en/blog-rtm-
 pitch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iffr.com/en/blog-rtm-pitch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotterdam\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:teatri-riflessi-2027-short-performance-competition@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Teatri Riflessi 2027: Short Performance Competition (12th
  edition)
DESCRIPTION:An open call for at least 10 short performances of maximum 15 m
 inutes for the 12th edition of Teatri Riflessi in Zafferana Etnea\, Sicily
 . THE FORMAT: the competition champions the short performance in its own r
 ight\, not as a reduction of a longer work nor as a sketch for a full-even
 ing adaptation\; its strength is the artistic immediacy and urgency it car
 ries. The framing connects ancient Greek theatre\, conceived as an outdoor
  competition for a large audience\, to the more provocative tendencies of 
 happenings and performance art that lean on the beholder's desire to parti
 cipate. STRUCTURE: semi-finalists perform on the evenings of Thursday 15 a
 nd Friday 16 July 2027\; the Programmers' Panel and the Scholars' & Critic
 s' Panel determine the finalists\, who perform again in the final on Sunda
 y 18 July. The panels bring together around 30 Italian and international a
 rtistic directors\, curators\, festival and theatre programmers\, journali
 sts\, critics and performing arts scholars\, many from the Teatri Riflessi
  Network and Anticorpi XL Network\; the full list is published in June 202
 7. Past partner organisations include Antistatic Festival (Sofia)\, ATER F
 ondazione\, BIG Festival\, Cantieri Danza\, Circuito CLAPS\, COORPI\, Danc
 e ICONS (Washington DC)\, Danza Urbana\, Derida Dance Centre\, EN-KNAP and
  Spanski Borci (Ljubljana)\, Fabbrica Europa\, Festival Ammutinamenti\, Cl
 uny Danse (France)\, Danza Canarias dentro y fuera (Tenerife)\, FIND Festi
 val\, Fondazione Armunia and Festival Inequilibrio\, Fondazione Claudia Lo
 mbardi per il teatro (Lugano)\, Fondazione Sipario Toscana\, Fondazione To
 scana Spettacolo\, Galway Dance (Ireland)\, Interplay Festival (Turin)\, L
 'Arboreto Teatro Dimora\, La Piccionaia\, Movimento Danza\, New Dance For 
 Asia International Festival (Daegu)\, Puglia Culture\, Toplocentrala (Sofi
 a) and Umbria Danza Festival. MONEY: each selected performance receives a 
 gross fee of EUR 500 to EUR 1\,100 depending on cast size\, plus a possibl
 e travel contribution of up to EUR 250. Awards are Best Performance EUR 1\
 ,200 (from the combined weighted scores of both panels\, the Jury of the F
 inal\, the Youth Jury and the Citizens' Jury)\, Best Dramaturgy EUR 500 an
 d the Scholars' and Critics' Award EUR 500 (both from the Scholars' & Crit
 ics' Panel)\, Best Direction EUR 500 and Best Performer EUR 500 (both from
  the Programmers' Panel)\, the 'Valentina Nicosia' Fund of EUR 500 (joint 
 decision of both panels)\, the 'Sandra Bressan' research fund of EUR 1\,80
 0 (awarded by the Citizens' Jury to reinvite a company to Sicily to work w
 ith the community)\, and the Youth Jury Award of EUR 300 to a semi-finalis
 t\, alongside the Audience Special Mention\, the Companies' Choice Award a
 nd the Technical Crew Award. Fees\, reimbursements and prizes are paid aft
 er the festival\, provided all regulations and deadlines are met. FEES TO 
 APPLY: none. Only selected companies pay a EUR 50 deposit on selection\, f
 ully refunded after the festival. RULES: performances should aim for 15 mi
 nutes\, with total stage occupancy including set-up and dismantling capped
  at 20 minutes. Multiple entries are allowed but need a separate form each
 . No major changes are permitted after selection\; minor adjustments\, esp
 ecially cast substitutions\, must be communicated in advance and authorise
 d by IterCulture APS. Works in languages other than Italian are welcome an
 d are presented with Italian and English surtitles prepared by IterCulture
  APS. APPLICATION: a digital form linked in Article 5 of the open call reg
 ulations\, with Annex A for dramaturgy (the complete script where one exis
 ts\, or for dance\, physical theatre and non-text work a short document on
  the dramaturgical research and choreographic structure) and a full video 
 recording of the complete work\; excerpts and teasers are not accepted\, a
 nd for rehearsed readings\, directorial notes on costumes\, lighting and s
 et design are mandatory. COMMITMENT: rehearsal attendance is compulsory\, 
 with the day assigned by the Competition Manager after selection\; compani
 es must arrive in Zafferana Etnea by their rehearsal day (rehearsals run 1
 3 and 14 July 2027) and stay until the festival closes at 23:30 on Sunday 
 18 July. Rehearsals and public events run mainly in afternoons and evening
 s\; the only compulsory morning commitment is the panel feedback session o
 n Sunday 18 July. Online information sessions are held on Google Meet on T
 uesday 22 September 2026\, with the English session at 19:30 CEST. Deadlin
 e 15 October 2026 at 5pm CET.\n\nOrganisation: IterCulture APS\nLocation: 
 Zafferana Etnea\, Sicily\, Italy. Open to Italian and international compan
 ies and artists. Semi-finals 15 and 16 July 2027\, final 18 July 2027\; re
 hearsals 13 and 14 July.\nAward: Gross performance fee of EUR 500 to EUR 1
 \,100 (VAT included) per selected short performance\, scaled by the number
  of performers on stage\, plus a possible travel contribution of up to EUR
  250 subject to available funding\, place of origin\, cast size and absenc
 e of external touring grants. At least 10 performances are selected. Compe
 tition prizes: Best Performance EUR 1\,200\; Best Dramaturgy\, Best Direct
 ion\, Best Performer and the Scholars' and Critics' Award EUR 500 each\; '
 Valentina Nicosia' Fund EUR 500\; 'Sandra Bressan' research fund EUR 1\,80
 0\; Youth Jury Award EUR 300\; plus non-cash awards (Audience Special Ment
 ion\, Companies' Choice\, Technical Crew). Panel members and Teatri Rifles
 si Network partners may also award special prizes in the form of artist re
 sidencies and touring opportunities. Application is free\; selected compan
 ies pay a EUR 50 deposit that is fully refunded after the festival.\nDurat
 ion: Festival participation 13 to 18 July 2027\, with mandatory rehearsals
  and presence until 23:30 on 18 July\n\nMore: https://www.iterculture.eu/e
 n/teatri-riflessi/tr2027/tr12/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.iterculture.eu/en/teatri-riflessi/tr2027/tr12/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zafferana Etnea\, Sicily\, Italy. Open to Italian and internationa
 l companies and artists. Semi-finals 15 and 16 July 2027\, final 18 July 2
 027\; rehearsals 13 and 14 July.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:next-art-ai-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI ART AWARD: NEXT ART AI 2026
DESCRIPTION:NEXT ART AI is an open AI art competition run by the HOBAN Cult
 ural Foundation\, welcoming participants of all backgrounds regardless of 
 career\, nationality or age\, and framed as a way to reflect on the future
  of AI art through new modes of expression and artistic experimentation. T
 WO CATEGORIES: AI IMAGE ART\, for works in a single-image format at 150dpi
  or higher\, submitted as JPG\, JPEG\, PNG or BMP up to 10MB\; and AI VIDE
 O ART\, open to a wide range of video formats including animation\, motion
  graphics and live-action footage enhanced or transformed using AI\, at 10
 80p or higher\, under one minute\, 30 or 60fps recommended\, stereo 48kHz 
 audio recommended\, as mp4 (h.264) or mov. Video entries are submitted as 
 a URL via YouTube\, Vimeo\, Dropbox or OneDrive\, or an alternative platfo
 rm if those are restricted in your region\; links that are inaccessible du
 e to privacy settings may be excluded from judging. WHO CAN ENTER: individ
 uals or teams of up to three including the representative\, though you may
  not submit both as an individual and as part of a team. Team representati
 ves create the account in their own name and all members submit a consent 
 form for personal data. Applicants under 19 need a guardian's signed conse
 nt. One work may be submitted per category. RULES ON AI AND ASSETS: work m
 ust be original and created by the applicant or team\, and must be image o
 r video art created using generative AI platforms. Works that have previou
 sly won an award in another competition are not eligible. Free or paid ext
 ernal assets\, game engines\, AI frameworks\, open-source tools and editin
 g software may be used freely\, but applicants must hold licences permitti
 ng commercial use for every element\, and work infringing third-party righ
 ts is excluded. Even where external assets and editing software are used\,
  the creative process must involve AI\, whether AI-assisted direction\, tr
 ansformation\, generation or other AI-based processes\, and the choice of 
 AI tools\, the scope and method of their use\, and the prompts themselves 
 are all weighed in evaluating the creative use of AI. TIMELINE: applicatio
 ns open 1 September 2026 and close 30 September 2026 at 11:59pm KST\, prel
 iminary round early October\, final round late October\, announcement and 
 ceremony early November\, exhibition late November 2026. Organised and hos
 ted by the HOBAN Cultural Foundation\, sponsored by HOBAN Group\, with Seo
 ul Shinmun and EBN as media partners. Details and schedule are subject to 
 change at the organiser's discretion.\n\nOrganisation: HOBAN Cultural Foun
 dation\nLocation: Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibit
 ion in South Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
 \nAward: Total prize pool of KRW 21\,000\,000 across 20 winners\, paid aft
 er deduction of applicable taxes and public charges. Grand Prize KRW 5\,00
 0\,000 (selected regardless of category)\; in each of the two categories\,
  First Prize KRW 2\,000\,000\, three Second Prizes of KRW 1\,000\,000 each
 \, and five Honorable Finalist awards of KRW 500\,000 each\; plus a HOBAN 
 Group President's Award of KRW 1\,000\,000. Winners also receive plaques a
 nd certificates\, online and offline exhibition opportunities\, and a feat
 ure on the official online platform. No entry fee is mentioned.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; exhibition late November 2026\n\nMore: https://next
 -art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://next-art-ai.com/en/apply/overview?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission\, with the awards ceremony and exhibition in Sou
 th Korea. Open to all regardless of career\, nationality or age.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emaf-2027-call-for-entries@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAF 2027: Call for Entries\, Film / Installation / Expan
 ded
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Festival (EMAF) in Osnabrueck invites su
 bmissions for its 2027 edition in three sections: Film (experimental films
  of all lengths and any theme)\, Installation (installative\, interactive\
 , spatial or sculptural media art works) and Expanded (performances\, live
  events or workshops). WHAT YOU GET: all films selected for the Internatio
 nal Selection are equal winners of the EMAF Award with EUR 400 prize money
  each\; films in the Features section (over 60 minutes) receive a EUR 250 
 screening fee\; curated programmes pay EUR 80-250 depending on length\; in
 stallations and expanded projects receive a EUR 500 fee with production co
 sts paid by the festival. Selected artists are invited to the festival wit
 h free accreditation\, three hotel nights (potentially longer if setting u
 p is required) and a contribution to travel costs. RULES: maximum 2 works 
 per artist\; only works completed in 2026 or 2027 are eligible\; no premie
 re status required\; works entered at previous editions will not be recons
 idered. Films up to 60 minutes are viewed for the International Selection\
 , films over 60 minutes for Features. Installation entries should relate t
 o the 2027 festival theme of the archive (as an instrument of knowledge pr
 oduction\, a site of critical intervention and a space for alternative vis
 ions of the future)\; Installation and Expanded entries must include a com
 prehensive description\, tech rider\, cost calculation and visual material
 s. Non-English-language works must have English subtitles for the selectio
 n screening. Submit digitally via the EMAF registration portal (no DVDs or
  physical media). Selection decisions are emailed from mid-March 2027. DEA
 DLINE: the call closes as soon as 2\,200 entries have been received\, or a
 t the latest on 15 December 2026\, so submit early. No entry fee.\n\nOrgan
 isation: European Media Art Festival (EMAF)\nLocation: Osnabrueck\, German
 y. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invited to the festival with free
  accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contribution to travel costs.\nA
 ward: All films in the International Selection are equal winners of the EM
 AF Award and receive EUR 400 each. Screening fees: EUR 250 for Features\, 
 EUR 80-250 for curated programmes depending on length\, EUR 500 for instal
 lations and expanded projects\; production costs for installations and exp
 anded projects are paid by the festival. Selected artists get free accredi
 tation\, three hotel nights (longer if setup requires) and a travel cost c
 ontribution. No entry fee.\nDuration: Festival in Osnabrueck\, spring 2027
 \; screening prints must arrive by 1 April 2027\n\nMore: https://emaf.film
 chief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invite
 d to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contr
 ibution to travel costs.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unlimited-partner-awards-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Unlimited: Partner Awards for Disabled Artists 2026/27 (U
 K)
DESCRIPTION:Unlimited\, the UK's flagship commissioning body for disability
  arts\, opens eleven Partner Awards for 2026/27 delivered with named partn
 er organisations including the Sainsbury Centre\, Norfolk & Norwich Festiv
 al\, Without Walls\, Cryptic\, Scottish Sculpture Workshop and Sherman The
 atre. The awards fund ambitious new work by disabled artists across theatr
 e\, performance\, digital media\, music and visual arts. WHAT YOU GET: awa
 rds of GBP 15\,000 to GBP 40\,000 (the Wales award is GBP 20\,000)\, total
 ling GBP 280\,000 across England\, Scotland and Wales\, supporting R&D thr
 ough to presentation and touring with a named partner. ELIGIBILITY: applic
 ants must be a disabled artist or lead a disabled-led company\, be based i
 n England\, Scotland or Wales\, be 18 or older\, and not be in full-time e
 ducation. ACCESS: application materials are provided in audio\, BSL\, Easy
  Read\, large print\, Scottish Gaelic and Welsh\, and access support for a
 pplying is available via commissions@weareunlimited.org.uk. DEADLINE: 28 S
 eptember 2026 at midday.\n\nOrganisation: Unlimited\nLocation: England\, S
 cotland and Wales\, UK. Open to disabled artists and disabled-led companie
 s based there.\nAward: Eleven awards totalling GBP 280\,000: eight awards 
 of GBP 15\,000 to GBP 40\,000 in England\, two awards of GBP 15\,000 to GB
 P 40\,000 in Scotland\, and one award of GBP 20\,000 in Wales. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: Award period 2026/27\; supports R&D through to present
 ation and touring\, varying per award.\n\nMore: https://weareunlimited.org
 .uk/opportunities/apply/partner-awards-2026-27/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://weareunlimited.org.uk/opportunities/apply/partner-awards-2026-2
 7/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:England\, Scotland and Wales\, UK. Open to disabled artists and di
 sabled-led companies based there.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:loewe-foundation-craft-prize-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261026T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: LOEWE FOUNDATION: Craft Prize 2027
DESCRIPTION:The 10th edition of the LOEWE FOUNDATION Craft Prize is open fo
 r registration until 15 October 2026. Established in 2016\, the prize rewa
 rds works combining technical excellence\, artistic quality and innovation
  in craft. WHAT YOU GET: the winner receives EUR 50\,000\, and shortlisted
  works are shown in an exhibition in Europe in spring 2027. DISCIPLINES: t
 extiles are explicitly listed among the eligible craft disciplines\, along
 side ceramics\, woodwork\, metalwork and other applied arts\, which makes 
 the prize a home for e-textile and material-innovation work with a craft d
 imension. ELIGIBILITY: entries must be original one-of-a-kind works made e
 ntirely or partly by hand\, created within the last five years\, and not p
 reviously awarded a prize\; applicants must be professionals at least 18 y
 ears old\, and individuals and collectives of all nationalities may apply.
  DEADLINE: registration closes 15 October 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisati
 on: LOEWE FOUNDATION\nLocation: Worldwide\; shortlist exhibition in Europe
  in spring 2027. Open to professional artisans aged 18 or over\, individua
 ls or collectives\, all nationalities.\nAward: EUR 50\,000 for the winning
  entry. No application fee.\nDuration: One-off prize\; shortlisted works s
 hown in an exhibition in Europe in spring 2027.\n\nMore: https://craftpriz
 e.loewe.com/en/craftprize2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://craftprize.loewe.com/en/craftprize2027?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\; shortlist exhibition in Europe in spring 2027. Open to
  professional artisans aged 18 or over\, individuals or collectives\, all 
 nationalities.
